From f283adeaaeeb01b379e789d63b607e47b136071d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:47:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PoUS: certified fraction falls with response latency instead
 of a pass/fail deadline

The bandwidth-audit bound tau(W) = (b_alt + b_rec) W / X, with W the measured response time, replaces
the 2 us yield requirement and the deadline. Defaults are the H100 figures of the PoUS research
(X = 4 GB, 3.1 TB/s, 55 GB/s over PCIe tiers). The toy engine reports the planned certificate at its
yield latency next to the one it earned; sweep.py tabulates the curve for several hardware profiles
and stress-runs the engine at 1.92 us, 16.4 us and 1 ms.

Co-authored-by: danielreuter <danielreuter@users.noreply.github.com>
